{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-325108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.25,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-325108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.25$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-325108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ad91b8d94543fcb407828a16a71dbc1cf39f64b6b74f9aa2f94a683d0816dc3"} {"question" "q-325108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-325108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25{y}^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-325108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x\\,y-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.25,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.25$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ad91b8d94543fcb407828a16a71dbc1cf39f64b6b74f9aa2f94a683d0816dc3"} {"question" "q-333098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25{y}^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333098" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.25\\,{x}_{\\text{new}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}-y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}+x,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2-1 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ad91b8d94543fcb407828a16a71dbc1cf39f64b6b74f9aa2f94a683d0816dc3"} {"question" "q-333114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{x}_{\\text{new}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}-xy,\\,y(0.5)=1.1\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(1).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0.5+0.5=1.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5(1){y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.1-0.5(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.5{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1.1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-1.6}{1.5}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(0.5)=1.1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1.1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & ≈1.066667 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.066667\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈1.07,$ rounded to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ad91b8d94543fcb407828a16a71dbc1cf39f64b6b74f9aa2f94a683d0816dc3"} {"question" "q-333251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.07"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-3x,\\,y(1.5)=-2.5\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1.5+0.5=2.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-2.5-1.5(2) \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=-2.5$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-5.5}{(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})-1}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1.5)=-2.5,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =-2.5 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =-2.464286 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈-2.464102 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈-2.464102\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-2.46,$ rounded to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ad91b8d94543fcb407828a16a71dbc1cf39f64b6b74f9aa2f94a683d0816dc3"} {"question" "q-333298" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-333298" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2.46"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"} {"question" "q-325108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "77af5865b71b93590b8ea872976e33e1bb99a0e29753a20f9b332ec0e07dbf70" "reviewer_session" "01a118ea-3923-70c2-acd9-0830602bde5f" "rationale" "Implicit Euler evaluates both arguments at the new point: y_new=y+0.25(x_new^2-y_new^2). Moving all terms left gives g(y_new)=0.25y_new^2+y_new-y-0.25x_new^2. This is original option 3, matching the authentic worked solution and successful grading. The stored expression differs only in formatting of the new subscripts and braces; the function argument, powers and signs agree exactly." "bindings" {"problem" "318658028c43f1d80bdb22f14941a178106b7b38a6b56fe910ea5f94b9664e34" "worked_solution" "0f9a24f4042f1335478440d581aadbbbe04a436fe1f6717bf9ba2c8097eda5a7" "original_field" "3275f3557b25e26ce632d78d87241536685ade3c95d0d4d6ee04885a0611126b" "reviewed_field" "b0f9340378eb26b93be0ea6990d1a74c66c8fd556ffe67ae8c4a6faed3a585ff" "raw_widget" "22c1a90abeb6de508bd62868bce23d31c582f8a1ed7620da15747d178a5b6d2a"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-325108-before.json" "sha256" "4605b01b4c507613b80b5ea27f4a5c9d5c391a8c148a5f76cea319ebfa86799a"} {"path" "q-325108-before.png" "sha256" "33145ecb10e1810e89176780130006824f4317f62b10c8d877a1f70b9f307e23"} {"path" "q-325108-after.png" "sha256" "e7af59a17dbc4aae999c7bd9edbdddbbd0949b5fdcb2852516e87218c0e771d3"}]} {"question" "q-325108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25{y}^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.25{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.25({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.25({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "77af5865b71b93590b8ea872976e33e1bb99a0e29753a20f9b332ec0e07dbf70" "rationale" "Implicit Euler evaluates both arguments at the new point: y_new=y+0.25(x_new^2-y_new^2). Moving all terms left gives g(y_new)=0.25y_new^2+y_new-y-0.25x_new^2. This is original option 3, matching the authentic worked solution and successful grading. The stored expression differs only in formatting of the new subscripts and braces; the function argument, powers and signs agree exactly."}] "usage" {"q-325108" []} "basis" 2318 "retractions" [[17592186229482 :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$y^{′} = x^{2} - y^{2}, y(0) = 1$\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx = 0.25$, the new value $y_{new}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g(y_{new}) = 0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g(y_{new})$ in terms of the new values $x_{new}$ and $y_{new}$, and the current value $y$?"] [17592186229482 :question/answer-fields 17592186227515]] "immutable_answers" [17592186227516 17592186227517 17592186227518 17592186227519 17592186227520] "immutable_fields" [[17592186227515 :answer-field/correct] [17592186227515 :answer-field/id] [17592186227515 :answer-field/key] [17592186227515 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
